# upstream/92-dead-code-iterative-initialization: dead-code analysis
# initializes nested regions from a worklist, so its native depth does not
# grow with the IR's nesting, and the solvers that load it keep a small
# stack. Run over operations nested 10,000 deep on a thread whose stack is
# 256 KiB, it finds the innermost block executable (dead-code.cpp). The
# analysis's initialization also walks the symbol tables
# (SymbolTable::walkSymbolTables), which recurses once per level of every
# operation at the pin and has no patch yet: until it has one, this check
# overflows there. The nesting is built in memory: mlir-opt's parser
# recurses on the same depth through each operation's parse hook, and
# SCCP's own sparse initialization recurses too, so through mlir-opt the
# analysis is never seen alone.
# Building a program against MLIR's libraries takes longer than a step.
step_limit=180
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
mlir_check "dead-code analysis: 10,000 nested operations on a 256 KiB stack, the innermost block executable" \
  "$here/dead-code.cpp" 10000
